Package: camtrapEvents
Title: Metadata-Aware Independence Filtering for Camera-Trap Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Samuel", "Awini", email = "winsamuel@hotmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Mar", "Cabeza", role = "aut"),
    person("Sandra", "Goded", role = "aut"),
    person("Ali", "Mahama", role = "aut"),
    person("Nathaniel N. D.", "Annorbah", role = "aut"))
Description: Collapses repeated camera-trap records into independent detection
    events. Conventional filters use a fixed time threshold alone, which cannot
    distinguish an animal lingering in front of the camera from the arrival of
    new individuals. This package lets the independence decision also use
    record-level metadata such as group size, age and sex counts, behaviour or
    individual identity, and provides tools to report how sensitive event totals
    are to the threshold and rule chosen. Implements the approach of Awini et
    al. (2026) <doi:10.1017/S0030605325102500>.
